From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: program LCSR_TX_DEEMPH on the A733, or Gen2 writes fail

With `usb-dwc3-a733-set-lluctl-bit30-for-gen2` an RTL9210 NVMe bridge links at Gen2. At that rate every write
fails on this board. The kernel logs USB Transaction Error events on the
bulk OUT endpoint from the first MiB on, and after 40-837 MiB one transfer
fails for good, uas error handling runs, and the device goes offline.
Measured on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-17:

  - The vendor 6.6 stack fails the same way.
  - usb-storage (BOT) instead of uas: 1854 errors in 35 s, and a device
    reset about every second.
  - 8 MiB chunks with pauses: 7-22 errors per chunk from the first one,
    flat over time.
  - Gen2 reads and Gen1 writes: zero (one run each).

The fault is therefore in the host-to-device direction at 10 Gbit/s, not
in uas, not heat. The same enclosure wrote 32 GiB cleanly on an x86 host
(2026-09-16).

Where the value comes from
--------------------------

The register is not in the A733 user manual (UM 18.4.4.2 defers the dwc3
registers to the Synopsys guide), so the evidence is silicon.

In the capture on both stacks, the dwc3 link-layer word 0x06A0D060 reads
0x34c2. A script sweeps it with the controller
retrained after each write: xHCI unbind/bind, which leaves the dwc3 core
alone. The metric is the number of trace-counted USB Transaction Error
events during a 32 MiB write:

  bits [1:0]  values tried                              errors / 32 MiB
  10          0x34c2 (3x), 0x34c6, 0x34ca, 0x0582,       50-66 (*)
              0x3502, 0x3482, 0x24c2, 0x44c2
  00          0x34c0 (2x), 0x34c4 (2x), 0x34c8,          2-7
              0x3540, 0x0600
  01          0x34c1 (5x), 0x34c5, 0x34c9, 0x34cd,       0
              0x0001
  11          0x34c3 (2x), 0x34c7                        link up, device
                                                          fails on the
                                                          first write

  (*) two of the three 0x34c2 runs (50, 66) were printed but not saved
      raw; the logged range of this group is 52-59.

Among the bits varied, only [1:0] had a measurable effect. Bits 2-3, 6-8
and 12-14 were varied singly, bits 4-5, 9-11 and 15 only together, and
bits 16-17 not at all. With 0x34c1 set by hand, 3x 2 GiB O_DIRECT writes
(414-418 MB/s) and a 4 GiB read (646 MB/s) gave zero transaction errors in
the trace; the journal count of uas/scsi error handling was 0.

What the register is
--------------------

Two upstream submissions define DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(n) = 0xd060 + n * 0x80
as the 18-bit TxDeemph that the controller drives on the PIPE4 interface
for Gen2:

  - Joy Chakraborty <joychakr@google.com>, "usb: dwc3: Program USB Gen2
    de-emphasis defined in PIPE4 spec" (2024-10-07, series in the first
    Link: below).
    Properties snps,tx_gen2_de_emphasis_quirk and
    snps,tx_gen2_de_emphasis, written in dwc3_ss_phy_setup(). It documents
    the split [5:0] C-1, [11:6] C0, [17:12] C+1. By that split 0x34c2 is
    C-1 2, C0 19, C+1 3.
  - Radhey Shyam Pandey <radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com>, "usb: dwc3: xilinx:
    Add support to program MMI USB TX deemphasis", v1 2025-11, v2 2026-03,
    v3 2026-04 (the other Link: lines). v3 reads snps,lcsr-tx-deemph in
    dwc3_get_software_properties(), supplied by its glue as a software-node
    property with no DT binding. It writes the register in
    dwc3_config_soc_bus() for every num_usb3_ports. Its Versal2 value
    0x8c45 has bits [1:0] = 01 as well.

Neither is merged. This patch follows Xilinx v3 in register name, mask,
UNSPECIFIED default, write site and port loop: the three register
definitions and the read-modify-write loop over the ports are taken from
Radhey Shyam Pandey's v3 patch. It differs in two ways:

  - It makes the value a DT property with a schema entry, read in
    dwc3_get_properties(). A raw register value in DT is something DT
    maintainers may question. It is done this way because the A733 is
    described through the generic flat glue, which has no match data to
    carry it.
  - It gates the write to DWC_usb31, the only core measured.

The upper 16 bits keep the reset value. The sweep does not fit the PIPE4
meaning of [5:0] on this PHY: a C-1 of 1, 5, 9 or 13 is clean, while 2, 6
or 10 fails and 3 or 7 loses the device. That is periodic in 4, not
monotonic, so which bits the PHY actually uses is not known beyond [1:0].

The vendor BSP never writes the register (in Alex Cao's 6.18 port of it,
alexcaoys/allwinner-bsp branch linux-6.18.y at 656a550c8267,
dwc3-sunxi-plat.c writes only LLUCTL(0)) and leaves the reset value that
fails. That is why its stack fails too. This patch is
where we go beyond it.

dwc3_config_soc_bus() runs inside dwc3_core_init(), which covers probe, a
dwc3 rebind and a host's system resume. Core soft resets outside it are not
covered (DRD role switch, gadget soft connect), same as for `usb-dwc3-a733-set-lluctl-bit30-for-gen2`; this node
is dr_mode = "host".

Verified: the value's effect, on silicon (the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-17, set by hand).
This patch: applies with --fuzz=0 on a fresh 6.18.36 tree carrying the
whole series. Not built, not run.

Pending on hardware, with a kernel carrying this patch and no register
written by hand:
  - LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(0) reads 0x34c1 after a cold boot and after a dwc3
    unbind/bind.
  - Gen2 writes and reads of several GiB complete with zero transaction
    errors.
  - Gen1 writes stay clean (bit30 cleared, retrained).

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20241007135508.3143756-1-joychakr@google.com
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20251119193036.2666877-4-radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260330190304.1841593-5-radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260429173050.1772377-5-radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com
Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
@@ -180,6 +180,7 @@
 #define DWC3_OSTS		0xcc10
 
 #define DWC3_LLUCTL(n)		(0xd024 + ((n) * 0x80))
+#define DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(n)	(0xd060 + ((n) * 0x80))
 
 /* Bit fields */
 
@@ -198,6 +199,10 @@
 #define DWC3_GSBUSCFG0_REQINFO(n)	(((n) & 0xffff) << 16)
 #define DWC3_GSBUSCFG0_REQINFO_UNSPECIFIED	0xffffffff
 
+/* LCSR_TX_DEEMPH: 18-bit TxDeemph driven on the PIPE for Gen2 */
+#define DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_MASK(n)		((n) & 0x3ffff)
+#define DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_UNSPECIFIED		0xffffffff
+
 /* Global Debug LSP MUX Select */
 #define DWC3_GDBGLSPMUX_ENDBC		BIT(15)	/* Host only */
 #define DWC3_GDBGLSPMUX_HOSTSELECT(n)	((n) & 0x3fff)
@@ -1184,6 +1189,8 @@
  * @num_ep_resized: carries the current number endpoints which have had its tx
  *		    fifo resized.
  * @debug_root: root debugfs directory for this device to put its files in.
+ * @lcsr_tx_deemph: TxDeemph for Gen2 operation, written to LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(n)
+ *	of every SuperSpeed port, or DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_UNSPECIFIED
  * @gsbuscfg0_reqinfo: store GSBUSCFG0.DATRDREQINFO, DESRDREQINFO,
  *		       DATWRREQINFO, and DESWRREQINFO value passed from
  *		       glue driver.
@@ -1428,6 +1435,7 @@
 	int			num_ep_resized;
 	struct dentry		*debug_root;
 	u32			gsbuscfg0_reqinfo;
+	u32			lcsr_tx_deemph;
 	u32			wakeup_pending_funcs;
 };
 
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -645,6 +645,20 @@
 		reg |= DWC3_GSBUSCFG0_REQINFO(dwc->gsbuscfg0_reqinfo);
 		dwc3_writel(dwc, DWC3_GSBUSCFG0, reg);
 	}
+
+	/* dwc3_core_init() calls this on probe and on resume */
+	if (dwc->lcsr_tx_deemph != DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_UNSPECIFIED &&
+	    DWC3_IP_IS(DWC31)) {
+		u32 reg;
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < dwc->num_usb3_ports; i++) {
+			reg = dwc3_readl(dwc, DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(i));
+			reg &= ~DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_MASK(~0);
+			reg |= DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_MASK(dwc->lcsr_tx_deemph);
+			dwc3_writel(dwc, DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(i), reg);
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 static int dwc3_core_ulpi_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
@@ -1887,6 +1901,10 @@
 	dwc->inv_sync_hdr_quirk = device_property_read_bool(dev,
 				"snps,inv-sync-hdr-quirk");
 
+	dwc->lcsr_tx_deemph = DWC3_LCSR_TX_DEEMPH_UNSPECIFIED;
+	device_property_read_u32(dev, "snps,lcsr-tx-deemph",
+				 &dwc->lcsr_tx_deemph);
+
 	dwc->lpm_nyet_threshold = lpm_nyet_threshold;
 	dwc->tx_de_emphasis = tx_de_emphasis;
 
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
@@ -214,6 +214,14 @@
       devices link at Gen1 on Allwinner A733.
     type: boolean
 
+  snps,lcsr-tx-deemph:
+    description:
+      18-bit TxDeemph value the controller drives on the PIPE interface for
+      USB 3.2 Gen2 operation (LCSR_TX_DEEMPH). When absent, the register keeps
+      its reset value.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    maximum: 0x3ffff
+
   snps,gfladj-refclk-lpm-sel-quirk:
     description:
       When set, run the SOF/ITP counter based on ref_clk.
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -1222,6 +1222,17 @@
 			 * stack, which sets it (0x06A0D024 = 0x408b8080).
 			 */
 			snps,inv-sync-hdr-quirk;
+			/*
+			 * LCSR_TX_DEEMPH(0). The reset value 0x34c2, which the
+			 * vendor stack leaves in place too, gives USB transaction
+			 * errors on every Gen2 write to an RTL9210 bridge (50-66
+			 * per 32 MiB) and drops the device within a GiB. Only
+			 * bits [1:0] moved the error count on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-17:
+			 * 10 -> 50-66, 00 -> 2-7, 01 -> 0, 11 -> the device
+			 * fails on the first write. 0x34c1
+			 * changes nothing but those two bits.
+			 */
+			snps,lcsr-tx-deemph = <0x34c1>;
 
 			/* Target for the connector's mandatory port@0 (HS). Inert:
 			 * dwc3 only builds a role switch when usb-role-switch is
